  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard",
  "published": "2026-10-13T09:10:01.397Z",
  "readmeFile": "PackageReadme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Requires exactly TokenGuard.Core 1.2.0, and OpenAI 2.14.0 or later. The package dependency on TokenGuard.Core is the exact version [1.2.0], so NuGet reports a mismatched Core version at restore. The summarizer reports the provider's finish reason, output tokens, and reasoning tokens, and the exception for an empty summarizer answer states them.\n\nBehavior changes come from TokenGuard.Core 1.2.0, with no signature changes: the default token budget is 40,000 instead of 25,000; tool-result masking moves its boundary in steps and the default placeholder of a masked result has a new text; a call that starts while another call on the same context is still running throws InvalidOperationException.\n\nKnown limits: summarization works with the built-in providers only, and a custom summarizer, compaction strategy, or token counter cannot be registered through the builder; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas and undercount pretty-printed JSON by 17% to 30% until the first provider report; one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.\n\nFull details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
